<Guide
  title="Cue Coach: Live BPM Counter for Sculpt and Barre Instructors"
  description="A BPM counter for fitness instructors. Cue Coach listens to music playing out loud, shows a live BPM, and pulses cue words on the beat."
  kicker="Cue Coach"
  heading="Cue Coach: a live BPM counter for class"
  crumb="Cue Coach"
>
  <div class="stack">
    <article class="card glass">
      <h2>It listens in the room.</h2>
      <p>Play the track out loud, from Spotify, Apple Music, YouTube or anything else. Cue Coach reads the tempo and shows a live BPM pulse so you can cue on the beat. We don't record, save or upload the audio. It stays on the phone.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card glass">
      <h2>Cue on the count you want.</h2>
      <p>Switch the pulse between half time, single time and double time, and pick the words you want to see: Up–Down, In–Out or Left–Right. Practice before class, or keep it on while you teach.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card glass">
      <h2>A BPM counter for fitness instructors</h2>
      <p>Cue Coach is a BPM counter for fitness instructors, not a music app. It listens through the microphone to whatever is playing out loud in the room: a speaker running Spotify, Apple Music, or any other source. There is no link to a music account. Tap Listen, set the phone down, and it shows a live BPM once it finds the beat.</p>
      <p>The circle then pulses cue words in time. Half is one cue every two beats, Single is one cue every beat, and Double is two cues per beat. The pairs are Up–Down, In–Out and Left–Right. We don’t record, save or upload the audio. It stays on the phone, and it stops when you tap Stop.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card glass">
      <h2>The class is still a Flow.</h2>
      <p>Cue Coach lives in the same app you plan in. Build the class as a Flow of Segments, choose from the 280+ movement library, and check the load with the intensity chart. On Apple Watch, the Flow shows the current segment, the movements in it, a timer, notes and what comes next.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Guide>

